# IMPORTANT THING TO UNDERSTAND

Salesforce automatically creates:

```text
Student__c
```

This becomes your table/object name.

Fields become:

```text
Roll_No__c
Class__c
Mobile_No__c
```

`__c` means:

```text
Custom
```

---

# STEP 4 — Create Apex Controller

Go to:

```text
Setup → Apex Classes → New
```

Paste this:

```java
public class StudentController {

    // Variables linked with form
    public Student__c stu {get; set;}

    // List to display students
    public List<Student__c> studentList {get; set;}

    // Constructor
    public StudentController() {

        stu = new Student__c();

        loadStudents();
    }

    // INSERT STUDENT
    public void saveStudent() {

        insert stu;

        stu = new Student__c();

        loadStudents();
    }

    // LOAD ALL STUDENTS
    public void loadStudents() {

        studentList = [
            SELECT Id,
                   Name,
                   Roll_No__c,
                   Class__c,
                   Mobile_No__c
            FROM Student__c
        ];
    }

    // DELETE STUDENT
    public void deleteStudent() {

        String studentId =
            ApexPages.currentPage()
                     .getParameters()
                     .get('sid');

        Student__c s = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM Student__c
            WHERE Id = :studentId
        ];

        delete s;

        loadStudents();
    }
}
```

Save it.

---

# Understand This Controller Properly

---

## 1. `Student__c stu`

Stores one student record.

Equivalent to:

```text
One row of table
```

---

## 2. `studentList`

Stores all students.

Equivalent to:

```text
SELECT * FROM Student
```

---

## 3. `saveStudent()`

Runs when Save button clicked.

```java
insert stu;
```

Adds record into Salesforce database.

---

## 4. `loadStudents()`

Fetches all students.

Uses SOQL:

```sql
SELECT fields FROM Student__c
```

---

## 5. `deleteStudent()`

Deletes student using record ID.

---

# STEP 5 — Create Visualforce Page

Go to:

```text
Setup → Visualforce Pages → New
```

Name:

```text
StudentPage
```

Paste:

```html
<apex:page controller="StudentController">

    <apex:form>

        <h1>Student Management System</h1>

        <apex:pageBlock title="Add Student">

            <apex:pageBlockSection columns="1">

                <apex:inputField value="{!stu.Name}" />

                <apex:inputField value="{!stu.Roll_No__c}" />

                <apex:inputField value="{!stu.Class__c}" />

                <apex:inputField value="{!stu.Mobile_No__c}" />

            </apex:pageBlockSection>

            <apex:commandButton
                value="Save Student"
                action="{!saveStudent}"
                rerender="table"
            />

        </apex:pageBlock>

        <apex:pageBlock title="Student Records" id="table">

            <apex:pageBlockTable value="{!studentList}" var="s">

                <apex:column value="{!s.Name}" />

                <apex:column value="{!s.Roll_No__c}" />

                <apex:column value="{!s.Class__c}" />

                <apex:column value="{!s.Mobile_No__c}" />

                <apex:column>

                    <apex:commandLink
                        value="Delete"
                        action="{!deleteStudent}">

                        <apex:param
                            name="sid"
                            value="{!s.Id}" />

                    </apex:commandLink>

                </apex:column>

            </apex:pageBlockTable>

        </apex:pageBlock>

    </apex:form>

</apex:page>
```

Save.

